      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right foot lump symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Lump remains and is somewhat annoying in enclosed shoes, especially cheap flats. Mild tenderness only when rubbed by a shoe; no pain at rest, itch, discharge, ulceration, or noticed colour change. Onset unclear; noticed this term or possibly last term. Size subjectively stable or possibly slightly increased, uncertain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right dorsal foot lesion examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 6–7 mm, firm, well-circumscribed, slightly raised tan-brown dermal papule with smooth surface at the dorsum of the right foot near the base of the fourth toe. Non-tender to light palpation, mildly tender with direct pressure simulating a shoe. Dimple sign present on lateral compression. No warmth, erythema, discharge, or cellulitis."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
